Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:05:32 +0000
Subject: Rewrite DB2-style DECODE into CASE in the parser

DECODE(e, s1, r1, s2, r2, ..., [default]) is rewritten to
CASE WHEN NOT (e IS DISTINCT FROM s1) THEN r1 ... ELSE default END,
so a NULL operand matches a NULL search value. The rewrite happens
before analysis, so calls with more than 127 arguments work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
